## Context

PR #309 (ticket 0246) added a `check-store` Makefile target -- `erg check
tickets/` over the real store -- and folded it into `make test`'s
prerequisites. So `make test` now does THREE things, not two: Go unit tests,
the shell integration suites, and a store-shape check.

`CONTRIBUTING.md:19` still describes `make test` as "Go unit tests + all shell
integration suites" -- accurate before #309, now incomplete. Surfaced by the
/gaze PR-review panel on #309 as a non-blocking doc-propagation gap.

A second-order nuance: `CONTRIBUTING.md:25` calls `make check` "an alias for
`make test` + `make validate`". Since `make test` now runs `erg check tickets/`
and `make validate` also runs it, `make check` checks the store twice. Harmless
(fast, deterministic) but the prose understates what `make test` does alone.

## Relevant files
- `CONTRIBUTING.md:19` -- the stale `make test` one-liner
- `CONTRIBUTING.md:25` -- the `make check` alias description (optional clarity touch)

## Actions
1. Update line 19 to mention the store-shape check `make test` now runs.
2. Optionally clarify line 25 so the double `erg check` under `make check` is
   not surprising.

## Test
- Doc-only change; no automated test. `make check` stays green.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] CONTRIBUTING.md:19 reflects that `make test` runs a store-shape check
- [ ] `make check` green on the clean tree
